README
======

CheckDate — a JOSM plugin

Author:  Till Butenschön <Till.Butenschoen@student.hpi.de>
License: GPL v2 or later (see the LICENSE file)

Purpose
-------
Speeds up stamping freshly-surveyed objects with the `check_date` tag
(https://wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Key:check_date).

It adds a "Set check_date" command to the Data menu (and, optionally, the
toolbar). Triggering it opens a small dialog whose text field is pre-filled
with today's date and whose OK button is the default. So the common workflow

    select object(s)  ->  trigger action  ->  press Enter

stamps everything selected with `check_date=<today>` in one undoable step.

A custom date can be typed instead. Accepted formats are the ISO-8601 forms
used by OSM: `YYYY`, `YYYY-MM` or `YYYY-MM-DD`.

Keyboard shortcut
-----------------
The action registers a shortcut entry but binds no key by default (to avoid
clashing with JOSM core or other plugins). Assign one under
Preferences > Keyboard Shortcuts — search for "check_date".

Building
--------
Maven (uses the JOSM core artifact from your local ~/.m2):

    mvn -pl checkdate package

The plugin jar is written to target/checkdate.jar. Install it by copying it
into your JOSM plugins directory, or use `ant install` (see build.xml).
